A||||4||GT Bastard||YOU MUST GO AUTOCROSSING!!!||||4||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||09-10-2000||08:54 PM||||Well, I finally went autocrossing today and I have to say it's f*cking nuts!  It's even more fun than I expected.  The course was setup on an airport taxiway and it was fairly long and fast.  But since the Autox was held 100 miles away from my home town, I didn't want to drive the Fiero(motor is on it's last leg, although new one is almost complete.)  My friend ended up driving his '86SE, 3.1 4sp and it was a blast to ride with him since he's and experienced driver.  I drove my '00 Xtreme S10 with a 4cyl auto and ZQ8 suspension and 4.10 gears. It handled very well, but I was totally outgunned.  It was one of the smaller events, and only the hard-core semi-professionals showed.  BMW M3, hopped up '84 Camaro, a few Stangs, race-prepped Rx7, a really cool BMW M5 factory race car, and a few others.  I got in a total of about 8 runs, and there's about nothing left of my tires!  I went from running 69 sec to 64.1 seconds on the course.  I never though a 4cyl pickup could burn this much rubber around a course though!  Brad was running a best of 59.1 and the big boys were running a 55.X to 50.X with their high-dollar mobiles.  I was actually really pleased with the results of my first run.  Everyone always says, slower is faster when you're a beginner.  I say, go balls-to-the-walls and don't hit the cones(I biffed one.)  But seriously, It's not as hard as it looks.  It feels really natural after a couple runs.  Anyhow, nuff ranting for now...  later all||||reg||4
Z||000001||Cheever2||09-10-2000||09:21 PM||||Did a few of those in my bachelor days with a 4-WD.  Met some good people, had a blast, won some plaques.  Very good experience.  Been thinking about doing it again.<BR>||||reg||14
